Concrete displaces the slurry and eventually hardens to form a foundation pile.

00:41:39.240 --> 00:41:46.710
200 of these piles work together to stop half a million tons of real estate from sinking into the ground.

00:41:48.860 --> 00:41:52.420
The building so far has gone down around 30 millimeters, which is slightly more than an inch.

00:41:53.240 --> 00:41:57.760
It's about the thickness of my thumb, which is a very small number for a building of this size.

00:42:00.670 --> 00:42:08.910
In just over 130 years, the skyscraper conquers all the forces of nature using the power of human ingenuity.

00:42:13.320 --> 00:42:18.390
But as buildings soar higher and higher into the sky, they become more vulnerable.

00:42:20.130 --> 00:42:23.550
Now, fear of terrorism threatens their existence.

00:42:27.730 --> 00:42:29.970
Today, a final technological...

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:34.920
leap forward keeps the occupants of the world's biggest skyscraper safe.

