answer is they don't.

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:08.060
contains nine very special rooms. Refuge rooms. Built from layers of reinforced

00:45:08.060 --> 00:45:13.380
concrete and fireproof sheeting, the walls of these rooms withstand the heat of a

00:45:13.380 --> 00:45:20.490
fire for two hours. Each room has a special supply of air pumped through

00:45:20.490 --> 00:45:29.240
fire-resistant pipes. Sealed fireproof doors stop smoke from leaking in. In the

00:45:29.240 --> 00:45:29.920
refuge room.

00:45:30.320 --> 00:45:35.300
Residents can seek shelter from a fire until emergency services bring it under control.

